          + "}\n"
          + "\n"
          + "/**\n"
          + " * A page to draw on and events to answer, for `--target browser`.\n"
          + " *\n"
          + " * A third profile beside `Core` and `Cli`, and only a browser provides it: a page capability\n"
          + " * that pretended to work in a terminal would be a lie, and the whole point of these structs is\n"
          + " * that reading one tells you what a program can reach.\n"
          + " *\n"
          + " * **An interactive application is a loop, not a set of callbacks:**\n"
          + " *\n"
          + " * ```wac\n"
          + " * page.render(\"<button id=\\'go\\'>go</button><p id=\\'out\\'></p>\");\n"
          + " * page.on(\"#go\", \"click\");\n"
          + " * while (true) {\n"
          + " *   Event e = page.nextEvent().wait();\n"
          + " *   if (e.id == \"go\") { page.setText(\"out\", \"hello\"); }\n"
          + " * }\n"
